WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.260
(upbeat music)
(crowd cheering)

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:06.210
- [Narrator] This is the
hottest sports ticket

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.800
in China right now.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.840
Thousands of people
from across the country

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.000
are cramming into an outdoor stadium

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.430
to watch this grassroots basketball league

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:17.310
that's become a nationwide phenomenon.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.290
We traveled to a remote mountain village

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:20.940
in the country's southwest,

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.510
the hometown of China's answer to the NBA.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.490
- The scene here rivals what you'll see

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:29.643
in a lot of pro basketball
games all across China.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:31.860
- [Narrator] The Cun-BA

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.100
or the Village Basketball
Association, provides a window

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.500
into China's passion
for the American sport

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.970
and has even attracted the attention

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.911
of professional NBA stars.

00:00:40.911 --> 00:00:42.780
(crowd cheering)

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.640
These amateur games, which
run well into the night

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.135
have blown up on social media in China.

00:00:49.135 --> 00:00:50.190
(crowd cheering)

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.230
We look at how this basketball court

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:55.050
has become one of the few
places where the US and China,

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:58.508
amid spiraling relations,
share common a ground.

00:00:58.508 --> 00:01:01.091
(gentle music)

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:07.230
Taipan Village is a small rural
village of just 1,200 people

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:11.310
in one of China's poorest
provinces, Gujiao.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:12.570
- There's no reason why you ever would've

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:13.710
heard of this village, and in fact,

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.420
most Chinese people had never heard of it

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.617
until a couple of weeks or months ago.

00:01:17.617 --> 00:01:18.780
(crowd cheering)

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.790
- [Narrator] And now it's
become one of the hottest spots

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:23.153
in China, because of the Cun-BA.

00:01:23.153 --> 00:01:24.028
(crowd cheering)

00:01:24.028 --> 00:01:27.945
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:30.900
- And it's really taken off here in China

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.400
not just in this village here

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.550
but all across this country
of 1.4 billion people.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:37.800
In Beijing and Shanghai,
all the big cities

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.020
have been tuning in watching live streams

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.852
on the Chinese version of TikTok
and it's really gone viral.

00:01:43.852 --> 00:01:45.690
(upbeat music)
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:48.510
One of the things that
makes this Cun-BA so special

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:51.480
is that none of these
players are professional

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.040
but what's so good about them

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.113
and what people love is the passion here.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.650
Another reason that the Cun-BA stands out

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:02.691
is it breaks the norm in
China's top-down sports system.

00:02:02.691 --> 00:02:03.540
(crowd cheering)

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:07.230
You have a system that
identifies athletes of promise

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.690
early on in their lives and
nurtures them through the system

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.060
often pays for their training.

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.560
This is totally different,
what you see here

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.873
this is amateur basketball.

00:02:17.432 --> 00:02:19.200
(gentle music)

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.300
And part of the appeal here
is not just the basketball

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.610
it's about the whole
festival atmosphere here.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.290
It's like a big karaoke night.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:27.540
They're doing singing,
there's dancing, there's games

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.849
there's all sorts of fun and festivities.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:32.409
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:32.409 --> 00:02:33.907
(upbeat music)

00:02:33.907 --> 00:02:36.270
(speaking in foreign language)
(crowd cheering)

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:37.650
The electric atmosphere here

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.260
it's even attracted some
attention in the NBA.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.730
Jimmy Butler of Miami Heat,

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.950
fresh off his NBA finals appearance

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:46.500
was here to take in these matches himself.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.860
He put on a traditional
ethnic minority outfit

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.403
and took the mic at the
center of the stage.

00:02:52.403 --> 00:02:57.403
(speaking in foreign language)
(crowd cheering)

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.210
- [Narrator] Stephon
Marbury, a former NBA star

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.460
now coaching in China's
professional league

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.560
visited Taipan Village recently

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.480
to draw attention to the potential talent

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.471
playing here in the countryside.

00:03:11.471 --> 00:03:15.210
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:18.150
- [Stephon] This can possibly
open up opportunities

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:21.630
for players who do play
in the Village League

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.370
for them to be able to get looked at

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.570
that need to be able to play

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.575
professional basketball for China.

00:03:27.575 --> 00:03:29.070
(upbeat music)

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.030
- [Narrator] Basketball is one of those

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:32.850
quintessentially American sports

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.430
and this is a time of US-China tensions.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.470
And yet, you don't feel that at all.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.334
People here love the NBA

00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:41.520
(crowd cheering)

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.620
Amid rising geopolitical tensions

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.540
this basketball court in Taipan Village

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:49.615
remains a rare arena of consensus
for the two superpowers.

00:03:49.615 --> 00:03:51.382
(crowd cheering)

00:03:51.382 --> 00:03:53.965
(upbeat music)

